<http://example.org/sen0414/ch06/diagrams> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "SEN0414 ch06 narrative diagrams - ABox"@en ; owl:versionInfo "1.0.0" ; dcterms:identifier "sen0414_ch06_diagrams_abox_v1_0_0" ;
    rdfs:comment "The chapter's authored diagrams as cme:NarrativeDiagram individuals: generated by sen0414_page_data_v2_6_0.py from sen0414_ch06_diagrams_v1_0_0.py, typed by the CME narrative-to-diagram mapping (a module of cme_standards_adoption_v1_3_0.ttl, CME 0.16.0)."@en ; owl:imports <http://example.org/cme/narrative-diagram> .

chx:Diagram_FindingAValue a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "How a program asks whether a value is in a list and where"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the Searching a list group: in and not in (an expression that evaluates to True or False), index (returns the position of the first match, raises a ValueError when the value is absent), and short-circuiting (a test on the left of and guards an expression on the right)" ; cme:elementCount 13 ;
    cme:accompanies "Membership" ; cme:accompanies "IndexMethod" ; cme:accompanies "ShortCircuit" ; rdfs:comment "the explanations describe what the programmer does in order - ask whether the value is in the list, ask for its position only when it is there, guard the item with a test of the length when the list may be empty - with choices on the way: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_RemovingItems a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Choosing how to remove an item from a list"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the Removing items group: del (when you know the index of the value you want to remove), remove (when you know the value itself; the first match only; a ValueError when it is absent), pop (removes the item at an index, by default the last, and returns it; an IndexError on an empty list)" ; cme:elementCount 14 ;
    cme:accompanies "DelStatement" ; cme:accompanies "RemoveMethod" ; cme:accompanies "PopMethod" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is a choice made step by step from what the programmer knows - the index or the value - and whether the removed item is needed afterwards, which is a workflow with decisions"@en .
chx:Diagram_ChoosingALoop a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Choosing the form of a loop over a list"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Workflow ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:ActivityDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6 and the Python documentation, the Looping over a list group: a for loop over the items, range(len(...)) for the indexes, enumerate for the index and the item, a list comprehension for a new list, and the warning not to change a list while a loop is walking through it" ; cme:elementCount 17 ;
    cme:accompanies "RangeLenLoop" ; cme:accompanies "EnumerateLoop" ; cme:accompanies "MutationWhileIterating" ; cme:accompanies "ListComprehension" ; rdfs:comment "the group compares forms by what the loop body needs - the item, the index, both, or a new list - and warns about one case, which is a choice walked through question by question: a workflow"@en .
chx:Diagram_ListContents a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "The life of a list: from empty to filled and back"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the List and Changing a list sections: the empty list [] contains no values; append, insert and extend add items; del, remove and pop take items away; the length of a list changes as items are added or removed" ; cme:elementCount 8 ;
    cme:accompanies "List" ; cme:accompanies "AppendMethod" ; cme:accompanies "InsertMethod" ; cme:accompanies "ExtendMethod" ; cme:accompanies "PopMethod" ; rdfs:comment "the explanations describe the states a list is in - empty, with items - and the events that move it from one to the next, append and its relatives forward and pop and its relatives back: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_NameAndList a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "A list and its names: shared, then copied"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:LifeCycle ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:StateDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the References and Copying groups: a variable holds a reference; the assignment copies only the reference, so two names refer to one list; copy.copy makes a separate list that shares the inner lists; copy.deepcopy copies the inner lists as well" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "Aliasing" ; cme:accompanies "ShallowCopy" ; cme:accompanies "DeepCopy" ; rdfs:comment "the passage follows one list through the states it is in as the program assigns, copies and changes it - one name, shared by two names, copied shallowly, copied deeply - and the events that move it on: a life cycle"@en .
chx:Diagram_ListArgument a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "What happens when a function receives a list"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the Arguments passage of the References section: when a function is called, Python copies the reference of the argument to the parameter variable, so for a list the code in the function modifies the original value in place" ; cme:elementCount 9 ;
    cme:accompanies "ListArguments" ; cme:accompanies "Aliasing" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between the calling code, the function and the list in an order that matters - the call, the copy of the reference, the append, the return, the print - which is an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_NestedCopy a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Copying a list that contains lists: what is shared"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:Interaction ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:SequenceDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6 and the copy module documentation: a shallow copy constructs a new compound object and inserts references to the objects found in the original; a deep copy inserts copies; repeating a list of lists repeats references to one inner list" ; cme:elementCount 11 ;
    cme:accompanies "ShallowCopy" ; cme:accompanies "DeepCopy" ; cme:accompanies "ReplicationAliasing" ; rdfs:comment "the passage is an exchange between the program, the copy module and the lists in an order that matters - the program asks for a copy, changes the copy, and looks at the original - and the answer differs between the two functions: an interaction"@en .
chx:Diagram_ListUses a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Who uses a list, and for what"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:SetOfUses ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:UseCaseDiagram ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the list data type and the searching and ordering branches: the programmer reads items by index, takes slices, replaces, adds, removes, searches and sorts; the interpreter raises errors for a bad index or a missing value; the user types the names the program checks and asks the Magic 8 Ball" ; cme:elementCount 16 ;
    cme:accompanies "List" ; cme:accompanies "Index" ; cme:accompanies "Slice" ; cme:accompanies "Membership" ; cme:accompanies "SortMethod" ; rdfs:comment "the passage lists what the programmer, the user and the interpreter do with a list - read, slice, change, search, sort, check, answer - which is a set of uses by actors, not a sequence"@en .
chx:Diagram_ChangesInPlace a cme:NarrativeDiagram ; rdfs:label "Changing a list in place: replace, add, remove and reorder"@en ; cme:hasPattern cme:TopicAndParts ; cme:hasDiagramType cme:MindMap ; cme:readFrom "chapter 6, the Changing a list branch and the Ordering group: replacing by assignment to an index; adding with append, insert and extend; removing with del, remove and pop; reordering with sort, reverse and shuffle; the methods change the list in place and return None, while sorted returns a new list" ; cme:elementCount 17 ;
    cme:accompanies "ChangingLists" ; cme:accompanies "ItemAssignment" ; cme:accompanies "AppendMethod" ; cme:accompanies "PopMethod" ; cme:accompanies "SortMethod" ; rdfs:comment "the branches classify one topic, the ways a list can be changed, by what the operation does to the list and list the choices under each - a topic and its parts, laid out to remember"@en .
